 ## Discord ops alerts
 
@@ -67,10 +67,14 @@ ## Discord ops alerts
 | Item | Detail |
 | --- | --- |
 | Env | `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` → `config('services.discord.webhook_url')` |
+| Mention env | `DISCORD_MENTION_ID` → `config('services.discord.mention_id')` (optional) |
 | Client | `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send($title, $message, $context = [])` |
 | Unconfigured | Empty/missing URL → silent no-op (safe for CI) |
+| Mention | Valid 17–20 digit Discord user ID → alerts end with `<@USER_ID>` on its own line; empty/invalid → no mention |
 | Failures | Non-2xx / transport errors are logged without the webhook URL; they do not throw |
 
+`DISCORD_MENTION_ID` pings the on-call user so alerts are not lost in a busy channel. Only a Discord snowflake (17–20 digits, surrounding whitespace trimmed) is accepted; anything else (including `@everyone`, `@here`, or values with embedded text/newlines) is silently ignored. The 1800-character limit still applies to the whole message, and room is reserved for the mention so it survives truncation.
+
 Call from jobs/handlers when a notable ops event occurs; do not wire every exception globally.
 
